rability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05083604339797024,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":67.6,"_gate_share_shrink":0.013208458609515139,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":33.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.011984260205322825,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":80.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00678,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Independence Realty Trust, Inc., an S&P 400 MidCap Company, is a real estate investment trust that owns and operates multifamily communities across non-gateway U.S. markets. IRT's investment strategy is focused on gaining scale near major employment centers within key amenity rich submarkets that offer good school districts and high-quality retail. IRT's main investment objective is to provide attractive risk-adjusted returns to shareholders through diligent portfolio management, strong operational performance, and a consistent return on capital through distributions and capital appreciation. Independence Realty Trust, Inc. was established in 2009 and is incorporated in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott F. Schaeffer | CEO & Chairman | Age 63 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 904 people. Revenue per employee of $728K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers, improving at 36%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Independence Realty Trust, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.6B market cap on $658M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +20% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 9.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 58% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5791085100033571},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Independence Realty Trust (IRT) Overvalued On Earnings Today?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-irt/independence-realty-trust/news/is-independence-realty-trust-irt-overvalued-on-earnings-toda","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793989317.469,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.951,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Independence Realty Trust (NYSE:IRT) Releases Earnings Results, Misses Estimates By $0.18 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/independence-realty-trust-nyseirt-releases-earnings-results-misses-estimates-by-0-18-eps.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793945177.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Independence Realty Trust (IRT) Shares Climbed, What Is Driving Fresh Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-irt/independence-realty-trust/news/independence-realty-trust-irt-shares-climbed-what-is-driving","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793896037.097,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.98,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Independence Realty Trust (NYSE:IRT) and Centerspace (NYSE:CSR) Head-To-Head Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2